   "id": "us-rally-oil",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "US stocks post their biggest rally in months as oil falls on Iran-deal hopes",
   "when": "Mon 9 Nov · US close",
   "what": "The S&P 500 closed at 7,549.94, up 2.35%, and the Nasdaq rose 2.74% to 25,253.14. Crude oil fell about 4% to 5%, to roughly $87 a barrel, on hopes of diplomatic progress in the US-Iran conflict. One report of a deal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz was denied by Qatar. The 10-year Treasury yield was around 4.87%, after topping 5.25% in early October. S&P 500 futures were up another 2.4% early this morning.",
   "why": "This morning your dashboard prices ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) at their 5 Nov NAV. The S&P 500 is 2.7% higher since then, so that gain is not yet in your numbers. K-GHRMF is also at 5 Nov, with a US healthcare proxy up 1.8% since. Fund NAVs usually catch up at the 11:30 refresh.",
