   "id": "nvidia-huang-probe",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Nvidia opens independent inquiry into its CEO; Korean chipmakers watch export rules",
   "when": "Mon 9 Nov · US session",
   "what": "Nvidia shares fell about 4.3% on Monday, while the Nasdaq rose. Nvidia's board said independent directors will examine whether CEO Jensen Huang was targeted by a foreign intelligence operation, after he admitted a personal relationship with a businesswoman US investigators have linked to chip-diversion probes. Nvidia says it has no reason to think secrets or national security were compromised. He stays CEO. Three House committee chairs asked for a closed briefing on 18 Nov. No new US restrictions have been announced.",
   "why": "Samsung and SK hynix supply memory used in Nvidia's AI chips. Tighter export checks could add compliance costs or delay shipments, which would reach SCBKEQTG and EWY. Nvidia itself is a very small direct holding. Seoul stocks cited the probe as one source of AI-sector uncertainty on Monday.",
